fib-gherkin v0.1.1: the argv override and the report sink of fib.test.run (package LT1 of docs/design/live-meshql.md, section 3.2)

Against fib-gherkin v0.1.0 (52e47fcf97007ebd8259b15df9a4fd24ff77f388). fibber's lib/fib/test/run.fib (this change) defines
`argv-override` (an `(Atom (Option (Vec str)))`: the words a live session's `test` op passes instead of `(args)`), `report-sink`
(an `(Atom (Option (fn :send (str) unit)))`: where the report goes instead of standard output) and `emit-report` (text to the sink,
or printed). gherkin.cli `:use`s fib.test.run, so the three names are in scope unqualified. Two hunks: `run` reads the override as
`fib.test.run/run-main` does, and the `--messages` stream goes through the sink as the report does. Nothing changes for `fibc test`
(its children never set the atoms). meshql-fib pins v0.1.0 in deps.lock: bump to v0.1.1 after the release.

--- a/src/gherkin/cli.fib
+++ b/src/gherkin/cli.fib
@@ ;; `--messages`: the run as Cucumber messages on standard output instead of fib.test's report; the status is 0 when every scenario held.
 (defun messages-status (pattern: str reg: (Registry w) o: Opts) -> i64
   (match (run-messages pattern reg o)
     ((Err m) (finish m))
-    ((Ok r) (do (print (. r fst)) (if (. r snd) 0 1)))))
+    ((Ok r) (do (emit-report (. r fst)) (if (. r snd) 0 1)))))
@@
-;; Runs the features and returns the exit status, 0 when every scenario held: the body of a spec's `main`.
-(defun run (pattern: str reg: (Registry w)) -> i64 (run-with pattern reg (vec (args))))
+;; Runs the features and returns the exit status, 0 when every scenario held: the body of a spec's `main`. The command line is `(args)`, or
+;; `fib.test.run/argv-override` when a live session set it (the `test` op of docs/design/live-meshql.md 3.2).
+(defun run (pattern: str reg: (Registry w)) -> i64 (run-with pattern reg (unwrap-or @argv-override (vec (args)))))

--- a/deps.fib
+++ b/deps.fib
@@
 {:name "fib-gherkin"
- :version "0.1.0"
+ :version "0.1.1"

Acceptance in fib-gherkin (a spec under specs/, run by `fibc test`): a program that sets `argv-override` to `["--only" ID "--format" "json"]`
and `report-sink` to a buffer, calls `(run "features/*.feature" (steps))` and reads the fib.test JSON of that one scenario from the buffer,
nothing on standard output; the same with `--messages` reads the message stream from the buffer. The existing specs stay green: nothing
of `fibc test`'s path changes. Requires a fibber whose lib/fib/test/run.fib has the hooks (the release that carries LT1).
